# Q2 round 2: replace the round-1 Q2 results (alpha-based mass etc.) in /output/report.json by the revised, measured set (s77a-h). Re-runnable: starts from out/report_before_q2r2.json (first run saves it).
import json,shutil,os
R='/output/report.json'; B='/workspace/out/report_before_q2r2.json'
if not os.path.exists(B): shutil.copy(R,B)
r=json.load(open(B)); res=[x for x in r['results'] if not x['evidence'].startswith('Q2:')]
O='/workspace/out/q2r2/'
A=lambda n,v,u=None:({'name':n,'value':v} if u is None else {'name':n,'value':v,'unit':u})
E=json.load(open(O+'s77e.json')); H=json.load(open(O+'s77h.json')); F=json.load(open(O+'s77f.json')); G=json.load(open(O+'s77g.json')); AA=json.load(open(O+'s77a.json')); D=json.load(open(O+'s77d.json')); Cc=json.load(open(O+'s77c.json'))
com=[A('distance','D=40 Mpc, 1"=194 pc; z from VSYS=2780 km/s radio-LSRK (s3b)'),
 A('data','Xb4d (0.94x0.74") and Xb4b (0.25") pbcor cubes HCN 3-2 spw27 / HCO+ 3-2 spw25, convolved (flux rescaled) to circular 1.05"; Xb4d hand-made tapered cubes and Xb4b manual cube as independent imagings'),
 A('baseline','per-pixel median of -900<v-VSYS<-450 km/s (radio velocity); field-aperture baseline for the coarse-channel cubes'),
 A('windows','blue -405..-150, red 180..320 km/s about VSYS unless stated')]
def add(q,t,v,u,un,conf,ev,extra=()):
    res.append(dict(quantity=q,target=t,value=v,uncertainty=u,unit=un,assumptions=com+list(extra),confidence=conf,evidence='Q2r2: '+ev))
def g(d,*k):
    for x in k: d=d[x]
    return d
# ---- 1 separability + geometry + null test
nl=lambda mol,sg,reg: G[f'{mol}|null|{sg}|{reg}']
add('Is the S dense-gas blue lobe separable from the disk (rotation / warp null test) and does its geometry match the CO outflow? (HCN, HCO+ 3-2)',
 'lobe 1.88" (365 pc) S of S; S and N nuclei and red feature for comparison',
 ('YES for the S blue lobe, NO for the nuclear wings. (1) Narrow-component velocity field at the lobe (Xb4b 0.25" per-pixel narrow-peak velocity, pixels >5 sigma): v0=+14 (HCO+) / -11 (HCN) km/s, range -41..+63 / -68..+49 km/s, gradient |grad v|=%.0f (HCO+) and %.0f (HCN) km/s/arcsec (components dv/dN=+27/+38, dv/dE-ish -19/-12), i.e. rotational smearing sigma ~15-18 km/s over the 1.05" beam. To place gas at |v_los|=180 km/s by smearing a >=340 km/s/arcsec gradient is needed (8-12x larger). (2) Beam-smeared rotation null model (every 0.25" pixel carries only a narrow Gaussian of sigma 25/40/60 km/s at its own measured velocity, smoothed exactly like the data): predicted wing flux (-405..-150) at the lobe = 0.000/0.003/0.008 (HCO+) and 0.000/0.002/0.005 (HCN) Jy km/s vs observed 0.31 (HCO+) and 0.30 (HCN) in the same Xb4b cube: rotation cannot produce the lobe wing. At the S nucleus the same null gives 0.02/0.14/0.40 (HCO+, sigma_n 25/40/60) and 0.01/0.05/0.13 (HCN) vs observed 0.18/0.10: the nuclear wings ARE reproducible by beam-smeared nuclear rotation + broad intrinsic lines (at N: 0.00/0.08/0.39 HCO+ vs 0.19), so only the lobe is separable. (3) E-W cut through the lobe (r=0.5" apertures, Xb4d@1.05"): where the wing is detected (flux >0.05 Jy km/s, -1.0"<=dE<=+0.5") the narrow-peak velocity is within -50..+47 km/s (no systematic E-W gradient; outside the lobe the narrow peak is noise dominated) and the wing centroid (-420..-100) is -190..-250 km/s at every such position: no rotating-disk pattern. (4) Geometry vs literature: our lobe is at PA 183+-2 (HCN), 190 (HCO+) deg, r=365 pc projected; Michiyama+2018 South-OF-Blue is 0.54" W, 2.23" S of their S nucleus = PA 194 deg, 445 pc (2" beam), HCN/HCO+ 1-0 detected in [-360,-180]; Sakamoto+2014 (ApJ 797, 90): S nuclear disk edge-on PA ~90 deg, outflow along the rotation axis (PA ~0/180), blue cone S, curving W with distance, opening ~20 deg, CO high-velocity emission peaking 1.8" (310 pc) from the nucleus on both sides, outflow axis inclination i=80 deg (70-85) FROM THE LINE OF SIGHT (flow near the plane of the sky; velocity factor 1/cos i = 2.9-11, 5.8 at 80 deg), Pereira-Santaella+2024 (A&A 681, A117) i~80 deg plane-of-sky, GOALS-JWST (arXiv:2403.14751) 20 deg from the sky plane (~70 deg from the LOS). Our lobe PA and distance agree with the CO outflow axis within the errors. The task note that the S outflow is "close to the line of sight" is not supported by these papers: it is close to the plane of the sky. Caveat: team-a p0006 (q3b_kin) gets the same answer (E-W gradient 35 km/s/arcsec -> expected sigma 62 vs observed 100-150 km/s); a tidal/warped extension of the disk with a velocity structure not seen in the narrow gas is not excluded by the data, but would need -180..-400 km/s with no counterpart in the narrow component.'
  %(((-19)**2+27**2)**.5,((-12)**2+38**2)**.5)),
 'gradient +-10 km/s/arcsec; null predictions are the central values for the three sigma_n','km/s, Jy km/s, deg','medium','s77g_disk_null.py -> out/q2r2/s77g.txt (null model, velocity field, E-W cuts), s75a PV (out/q2), s74a; literature: Sakamoto+2014 arXiv:1403.7117 Sect 5.2/Table 8; Michiyama+2018 arXiv:1810.04821 Table 1,3; Pereira-Santaella+2024 arXiv:2309.06486',
 [A('inclination','i (outflow axis from LOS) = 80 deg fiducial, 70-85 deg range (Sakamoto+2014)'),A('null model','narrow Gaussian sigma_n 25/40/60 km/s per pixel, pixel = >5 sigma at 0.25", velocities = narrow-peak parabola')])
