r['caveats'].append("Q2r2: the flux scale of the residual-dominated wing is +25%/-10% (cross-imaging spread of Xb4d/tapered/manual cubes and a synthetic-uv epsilon of 0.73-0.95 whose sign/size depends on the unknown uv coverage; Xb4b gives half the HCN flux); 'lower limit' is no longer claimed. The non-LTE dense mass is a single-zone model that does not reproduce the HCN 3-2/1-0 ratio (HCN IR pumping, two phases, or HCN overabundance not modelled), is dominated by the unknown abundance (X 1e-9..1e-8, factor 10), by the density (1e5 vs 1e6) and by a clump-column degeneracy (capped at 3e23 cm-2); the 1-0 fluxes are Michiyama's (different aperture/beam, +-30%). Mdot depends on i (70-85 deg; i from the line of sight, flow near the plane of the sky), v (broad |v| 134 vs wing 283 km/s), R and the formula (x3): 1.5 dex, and is not a steady-state measurement. Gaussian decompositions: HCN and HCO+ require different kinematics and HDO vs HCN-rich gas is not decided. The null test uses pixels >5 sigma at 0.25 arcsec and thus misses faint extended emission, but an analytic bound (>=340 km/s/arcsec) gives the same conclusion; the nuclear wings are not separable from rotation. The red feature's origin (S counter-lobe, N outflow, Bridge) is open. Confirmation needs the 1-0/2-1 lines of the lobe at matched resolution (HCN 2-1 with Xb55 is too coarse), HCN v2=1 / H13CN to test pumping and opacity, and CO at 0.2-0.5\" for a window-matched dense fraction.")
